  "body": "## Summary / \u53d8\u66f4\u6458\u8981\n\nAfter original-v2 migration and cluster restart, incomplete recovery proof could escape as HTTP 400 and stop history reads. Preserve public `ErrNotReady` for the two transient proof states so the existing retryable 503 contract survives RPC boundaries; retain permanent errors, quorum proof and write fencing.\n\nCandidate Linux regression also exposed a nested MQTT cancellation race: asynchronous propagation could return pending-drain after the original caller canceled. Carry private scope ancestry and synchronously check every parent and Owner gate before further effects, preserving deadlines and uncertainty semantics. Correct the replication test router to inject faults per coalesced item; no replication product behavior or assertion threshold is weakened.\n\nInclude complete-history migration assertions, authenticated self-chat/restart coverage, cross-node authentication fixture corrections, and credential-free Linux default-suite plus process E2E acceptance. The runner retains original outcomes and cleans only its owned session, including independently grouped nodes.\n\nThis 28-file integration PR keeps the extensive evidence on `codex/v3-rc-qualification`. Initial head `5f3ecdf93e762a1b1551b44977a44f2e63c97802` matched qualified product `ef798352c40a94e57f768f76b2f4713712f827fe`; the MQTT repair changes product code, so updated head `7e9da7df100d193330b3d509cfdbe079ea32a6f8` is receiving fresh acceptance. No tag, cloud purchase, production channel enablement, or protected Review/Issue Agent control change is included.\n\n## Release notes / \u53d1\u5e03\u8bf4\u660e\n\n- [x] I added every user-visible change to `CHANGELOG.md` under `[Unreleased]`.\n- [ ] This pull request has no user-visible change. I explained why below and a maintainer added the `skip-changelog` label.\n\n## Verification / \u9a8c\u8bc1\n\n- Original migration repair: five topologies, 55 complete-history observations, cold/hot reads and Channel failover passed. [Frozen report](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/blob/32d402f7625c36f5667a290ec95c045f5f35937c/docs/reports/2026-10-20-v3-migration-recovery-repair.md).\n- Original product floor: [20/20 Linux results](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/actions/runs/39453556254), 43,800 completed, zero errors/drops, maximum P99 75.80928 ms. This remains evidence for that exact source, not certification of the new MQTT change.\n- Initial integration [default-suite run](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/actions/runs/39546957124) failed the MQTT cancellation and replication-fixture assertions; dependent E2E was skipped. Original exit 1, full output and verified Linux session cleanup are retained. Other initial SDK/Manager/native/three-node runs passed, but do not override this failure.\n- MQTT: deterministic delayed-cancellation case failed before the fix; the 19-case contention matrix passed three times, the full package passed, and related race checks passed. Assertions require no post-cancel qualification reads or source seal and preserve Removing/progress state. Independent review found no actionable issue.\n- Replication fixture: real batcher regression failed before the fix; original saturation scenario changed from 6 failures in 150 observed runs to 150/150 pass, followed by full-package and focused race pass. Exact 66 retained obligations and durable follower catch-up remain required.\n- Self-chat local evidence: single-node and three-node clusters passed 12 ACKs, 12 complete-history observations and two restarts; initial pagination/Close fixture failures retained. Duplicate real-time frames follow existing client deduplication semantics.\n- `flow-doc-contracts` passed after regenerating its index; earlier workflow/static/actionlint checks and real-process runner failure probes are retained. Linux fault-injection coverage is not inferred from ordinary successful cleanup.\n- Fresh updated-source candidate/SDK/Manager/native/three-node CI is in progress. [Ten-minute 500 SEND/s acceptance](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/actions/runs/39548576246) and [fixed full Linux conversation matrix](https://github.com/WuKongIM/WuKongIM/actions/runs/39548584710) were each dispatched once for this new head. Results will be recorded before candidate integration is called qualified.\n\nThe CPU attribution experiment does not establish beta-to-candidate non-regression and is not a new release gate. The agreed formal RC long-run stages and signed stable native-package publication remain pending; this PR does not claim formal v3 readiness. MQTT remains a default-off development preview.\n",
